IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc8-sch3`

-- Tests for ssc8-sch3.l4 (Schedule 3, contribution conditions). Every expected value is written
-- by hand from the text of the paragraph named beside the assertion, before the run.
-- Illustrative figures only: a lower earnings limit of 100 a week and a qualifying earnings factor
-- of 3000 make 25 times the limit 2500, 50 times 5000. They are test inputs, not the Act's figures.

§ `Tests for Schedule 3`

§§ `Builders (test helpers)`

-- A year of the record: the calendar year it begins in, its lower earnings limit, its qualifying
-- earnings factor, paid actually, paid before the relevant time, paid or credited, earnings credited,
-- and the two earnings factors.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      lel IS A NUMBER
      qef IS A NUMBER
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
      before IS A BOOLEAN
      poc IS A BOOLEAN
      cred IS A BOOLEAN
      ef1 IS A NUMBER
      ef2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
`sch 3 test a year` MEANS
    `sch 3 pt I a year of the record` OF (`Earnings limits` OF (`Tax year` OF y), lel, 0, 0, 0), paid, before, poc, cred, ef1, ef2, qef

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
`sch 3 test good year` MEANS `sch 3 test a year` y 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000

GIVEN y1 IS A `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
      y2 IS A `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
      y3 IS A `sch 3 pt I a year of the record`
GIVETH A `sch 3 pt I para 2 the last three complete years`
`sch 3 test three years` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 2 the last three complete years` OF y1, y2, y3

`sch 3 test all good` MEANS `sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test good year` 2022) (`sch 3 test good year` 2021) (`sch 3 test good year` 2020)

§§ `Paragraph 2(6) -- the relevant time and the relevant benefit year`

-- (6)(a): the relevant time is the day in respect of which benefit is claimed.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(a) the relevant time` (Date 15 3 2024) EQUALS Date 15 3 2024

-- s 21(6): a benefit year begins on the first Sunday in January. 1 Jan 2024 was a Monday, so the first Sunday is 7 Jan.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the first Sunday in January of the calendar year` 2024 EQUALS Date 7 1 2024
-- 1 Jan 2023 was a Sunday.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the first Sunday in January of the calendar year` 2023 EQUALS Date 1 1 2023
-- 1 Jan 2022 was a Saturday, so the first Sunday is 2 Jan.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the first Sunday in January of the calendar year` 2022 EQUALS Date 2 1 2022
-- 1 Jan 2021 was a Friday, so the first Sunday is 3 Jan.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the first Sunday in January of the calendar year` 2021 EQUALS Date 3 1 2021

-- (6)(b): a period of incapacity that began in March 2024 began in the benefit year that began in January 2024.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the calendar year in which the relevant benefit year begins` (Date 10 3 2024) EQUALS 2024
-- the Saturday before the first Sunday belongs to the benefit year before.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the calendar year in which the relevant benefit year begins` (Date 6 1 2024) EQUALS 2023
-- the first Sunday itself belongs to the new one.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the calendar year in which the relevant benefit year begins` (Date 7 1 2024) EQUALS 2024
-- 1 Jan 2023 is itself the first Sunday of 2023.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the calendar year in which the relevant benefit year begins` (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS 2023
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the calendar year in which the relevant benefit year begins` (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS 2022
-- 1 Jan 2022 (a Saturday) falls before 2 Jan 2022, so in the benefit year that began in January 2021.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the calendar year in which the relevant benefit year begins` (Date 1 1 2022) EQUALS 2021
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(6)(b) the calendar year in which the relevant benefit year begins` (Date 2 1 2022) EQUALS 2022

§§ `Paragraph 2(2)(a) -- which years are the last three complete years`

-- Benefit year beginning in January 2024: the last complete tax year is 2022-23 (it ended on 5 April 2023).
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(a) the records are the last three complete years` `sch 3 test all good` 2024 EQUALS TRUE
-- the same records are not the last three complete years of a benefit year beginning in 2025.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(a) the records are the last three complete years` `sch 3 test all good` 2025 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(a) the records are the last three complete years` (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test good year` 2021) (`sch 3 test good year` 2022) (`sch 3 test good year` 2020)) 2024 EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- the per-year tests`

-- (2)(a): actually paid AND paid before the relevant time.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(a) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid in time for the year` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(a) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid in time for the year` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(a) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid in time for the year` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS FALSE

-- (2)(b): the earnings factor is "not less than" 25 times the year's lower earnings limit: 2500 yes, 2499 no.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(b) the earnings factor is at least 25 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(b) the earnings factor is at least 25 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2499 5000) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2)(b) the earnings factor is at least 25 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2501 5000) EQUALS TRUE

-- (3)(a): paid or credited contributions; or (1987-88 or any subsequent year) credited earnings.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2500 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 1987 100 3000 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2500 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 1986 100 3000 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2500 5000) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 1986 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS FALSE

-- (3)(b): 50 times: 5000 yes, 4999 no.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(b) the earnings factor is at least 50 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3)(b) the earnings factor is at least 50 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 4999) EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 2(2) -- the first condition`

-- all three years good.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2024 `sch 3 test all good` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- only the third last year (2020) is good: "one of the last three complete years" is enough.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2499 5000) (`sch 3 test good year` 2020)) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) in one year and (b) in another: "that year's lower earnings limit" is the year of (a), so this fails (fork F-S3-1).
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2499 5000) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 3000 5000) (`sch 3 test a year` 2020 100 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 3000 5000)) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- contributions paid but not before the relevant time.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000) (`sch 3 test a year` 2020 100 3000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 2500 5000)) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8): regulations take the first condition to be satisfied.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0) (`sch 3 test a year` 2020 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0)) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- records that are not the last three complete years of benefit year 2025: not answered.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2025 `sch 3 test all good` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- but regulations under (8) decide it whatever the records say.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2025 `sch 3 test all good` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `Paragraph 2(3) -- the second condition`

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3) the second condition is satisfied` 2024 `sch 3 test all good` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 4999 in the second last year.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3) the second condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test good year` 2022) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 4999) (`sch 3 test good year` 2020)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no contributions and no credit in the last year.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3) the second condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2500 5000) (`sch 3 test good year` 2021) (`sch 3 test good year` 2020)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- earnings credited instead of contributions (a year from 1987-88): enough.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3) the second condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2500 5000) (`sch 3 test good year` 2021) (`sch 3 test good year` 2020)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the third last year does not matter to the second condition.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3) the second condition is satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test good year` 2022) (`sch 3 test good year` 2021) (`sch 3 test a year` 2020 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- records that are not the last two complete years of benefit year 2025: not answered.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(3) the second condition is satisfied` 2025 `sch 3 test all good` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 2(1) -- both conditions (seam S1 for short-term incapacity benefit)`

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2 the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit are satisfied` 2024 `sch 3 test all good` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- first condition fails, second holds.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2 the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit are satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test a year` 2022 100 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000) (`sch 3 test a year` 2020 100 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000)) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- first condition holds, second fails.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2 the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit are satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test good year` 2022) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 4999) (`sch 3 test good year` 2020)) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- records for the wrong years: the first condition and the second are both not answered.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2 the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit are satisfied` 2025 `sch 3 test all good` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the third last record is for the wrong year (2000): the first condition is not answered, the second fails: a JUST FALSE decides.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2 the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit are satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test good year` 2022) (`sch 3 test a year` 2021 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2500 4999) (`sch 3 test good year` 2000)) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the third last record is for the wrong year (2000): the first condition is not answered, the second holds: not answered.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2 the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit are satisfied` 2024 (`sch 3 test three years` (`sch 3 test good year` 2022) (`sch 3 test good year` 2021) (`sch 3 test good year` 2000)) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 2(7), (9)`

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(7) the previous claim is disregarded` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(7) the previous claim is disregarded` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(7) the previous claim is disregarded` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(7) the previous claim is disregarded` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(7) the previous claim is disregarded` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the thing is a benefit for sub-paragraph (8)` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) a benefit under Parts II to V of this Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the thing is a benefit for sub-paragraph (8)` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) a benefit under Parts VII to XII of this Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the thing is a benefit for sub-paragraph (8)` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) credits under regulations under section 22(5)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the thing is a benefit for sub-paragraph (8)` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) credits under regulations under section 22(5)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "includes": a benefit the sub-paragraph does not name is not answered.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the thing is a benefit for sub-paragraph (8)` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) some other benefit` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the change is a modification` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) an addition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the change is a modification` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) an omission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the change is a modification` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) an amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) the change is a modification` `sch 3 pt I para 2(9) some other change` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5(1) -- which benefits this paragraph sets conditions for`

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `widowed mother's allowance` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `widowed parent's allowance` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `widow's pension` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Category A, and paragraph 5A applies to it: excluded by "other than one in relation to which paragraph 5A applies".
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `Category A retirement pension` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `Category A retirement pension` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `Category A retirement pension` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a benefit the list does not name: not answered.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `child's special allowance` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5(5), (8) -- relevant years and the working life`

-- the tax year runs 6 April to 5 April.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the tax year in which the day falls` (Date 5 4 2010) EQUALS `Tax year` OF 2009
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the tax year in which the day falls` (Date 6 4 2010) EQUALS `Tax year` OF 2010
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the tax year in which the day falls` (Date 31 12 2010) EQUALS `Tax year` OF 2010
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the tax year in which the day falls` (Date 1 1 2011) EQUALS `Tax year` OF 2010

-- attained pensionable age on 5 April 2010 (tax year 2009-10): 2008-09 is a relevant year, 2009-10 is not.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the year is a relevant year` (`sch 3 test good year` 2008) (Date 5 4 2010) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the year is a relevant year` (`sch 3 test good year` 2009) (Date 5 4 2010) EQUALS FALSE
-- on 6 April 2010 (tax year 2010-11): 2009-10 is a relevant year, 2010-11 is not.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the year is a relevant year` (`sch 3 test good year` 2009) (Date 6 4 2010) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(5) the year is a relevant year` (`sch 3 test good year` 2010) (Date 6 4 2010) EQUALS FALSE

-- (8): the working life runs from the tax year in which the contributor attained 16 (inclusive) to the tax year in which they attained pensionable age (exclusive).
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(8) the number of years of the contributor's working life` (Date 15 6 1960) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS 65
-- 16th birthday on 5 April 1976 is in tax year 1975-76; on 6 April 1976 in 1976-77.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(8) the number of years of the contributor's working life` (Date 5 4 1976) (Date 5 4 2041) EQUALS 65
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(8) the number of years of the contributor's working life` (Date 6 4 1976) (Date 5 4 2041) EQUALS 64
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(8) the year is in the contributor's working life` (`sch 3 test good year` 1960) (Date 15 6 1960) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(8) the year is in the contributor's working life` (`sch 3 test good year` 1959) (Date 15 6 1960) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(8) the year is in the contributor's working life` (`sch 3 test good year` 2024) (Date 15 6 1960) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(8) the year is in the contributor's working life` (`sch 3 test good year` 2025) (Date 15 6 1960) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 5(2) -- the first condition`

-- (2)(a),(b): actually paid, and the earnings factor reaches the qualifying earnings factor (3000 here): 3000 yes, 2999 no.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches the qualifying earnings factor` (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 3000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches the qualifying earnings factor` (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2999 3000) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches the qualifying earnings factor` (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 3000) EQUALS FALSE

-- years: 2005 qualifies, 2006 is 1 short, 2009 qualifies but is a relevant year only if pensionable age is attained after 5 April 2010.
`sch 3 test five-two years` MEANS LIST (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 3000), (`sch 3 test a year` 2006 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2999 3000), (`sch 3 test a year` 2009 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 3000)
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the number of relevant years that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` `sch 3 test five-two years` (Date 5 4 2010) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the number of relevant years that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` `sch 3 test five-two years` (Date 6 4 2010) EQUALS 2

-- (6): entitled to long-term incapacity benefit in the year of attaining pensionable age or the year before.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6) the first condition is taken to be satisfied` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6) the first condition is taken to be satisfied` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6B): an addition under section 2(1)(b) or 4(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6B) the allowance is main phase employment and support allowance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6B) the allowance is main phase employment and support allowance` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6A)
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6A) the first condition is taken to be satisfied` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6A) the first condition is taken to be satisfied` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6A) the first condition is taken to be satisfied` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(6A) the first condition is taken to be satisfied` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) with (6) and (6A)
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied` 1 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied` 0 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied` 0 (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied` 0 (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied` 0 NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied` 0 (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied` 2 NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `Paragraph 5(3), (7) -- the second condition`

-- working life 1 Jan 1970 (16th birthday, tax year 1969) to 1 Jan 2035 (tax year 2034): years 1969 to 2033.
-- 2000 and 2002 count; 2001 has an earnings factor 1 short; 1980 has only credited earnings, which do not count before 1987-88; 2040 is outside the working life.
`sch 3 test working life years` MEANS LIST (`sch 3 test a year` 2000 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 3000), (`sch 3 test a year` 2001 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 2999), (`sch 3 test a year` 2002 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 3000), (`sch 3 test a year` 1980 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 3000), (`sch 3 test a year` 2040 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 3000)
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3) the number of years of the working life that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` `sch 3 test working life years` (Date 1 1 1970) (Date 1 1 2035) EQUALS 2

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 1986 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 3000) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3)(a) the year has contributions paid or credited, or earnings credited` (`sch 3 test a year` 1987 100 3000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 3000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3)(b) the earnings factor reaches the qualifying earnings factor` (`sch 3 test a year` 2000 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 3000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3)(b) the earnings factor reaches the qualifying earnings factor` (`sch 3 test a year` 2000 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 2999) EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3) the second condition is satisfied` 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3) the second condition is satisfied` 3 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3) the second condition is satisfied` 39 39 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(3) the second condition is satisfied` 39 38 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (7): requisite number 4, 2 complying years, 2 home-responsibility years among the other years: half is 2 and 2 + 2 covers all 4.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 4 2 2 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A does not apply to the benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one of the two other years is not a home-responsibility year.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 4 2 1 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A does not apply to the benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- complying years short of half.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 4 1 3 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A does not apply to the benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- requisite number 5: half is 2.5, so 3 complying years are enough and 2 are not.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 5 3 2 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A does not apply to the benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 5 2 3 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A does not apply to the benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 5 3 1 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A does not apply to the benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "But nothing in this sub-paragraph applies in relation to any benefit to which section 23A above applies."
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 4 4 0 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A applies to the benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied` 4 2 2 `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A applies to the benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 5 as a whole (seam S1)`

-- sets out, first, (7), (3) in that order of arguments.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- paragraph 5 does not set the conditions for this benefit, or it is not answered whether it does.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5A -- the 30-year condition`

-- (1)(a): Category A where the contributor attains pensionable age on or after 6 April 2010.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` `Category A retirement pension` (Date 6 4 2010) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` `Category A retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2010) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(b): Category B in the cases provided for by ss 48A to 51ZA.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2010) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2010) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- any other benefit: the list is not closed.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` `widow's pension` (Date 6 4 2010) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): at least 30 years.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(2) the contribution condition is satisfied` 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(2) the contribution condition is satisfied` 29 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(2) the contribution condition is satisfied` 35 EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): regulations modify the condition so that it is met.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the paragraph does not apply to this benefit: it sets no condition.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- child's special allowance`

-- (2): a relevant year is a year ending before the day the contributor attained pensionable age or died under that age.
-- The year 2009-10 ends on 5 April 2010.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(2) the year is a relevant year` (`sch 3 test good year` 2008) (Date 5 4 2010) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(2) the year is a relevant year` (`sch 3 test good year` 2009) (Date 5 4 2010) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(2) the year is a relevant year` (`sch 3 test good year` 2009) (Date 6 4 2010) EQUALS TRUE

-- (1): actually paid AND the earnings factor reaches 50 times the lower earnings limit: 5000 yes, 4999 no.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(1) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches 50 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(1) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches 50 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 4999 5000) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(1) contributions of a relevant class were actually paid and the earnings factor reaches 50 times the lower earnings limit` (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000) EQUALS FALSE

`sch 3 test para 6 years` MEANS LIST (`sch 3 test a year` 2005 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000), (`sch 3 test a year` 2006 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 4999 5000), (`sch 3 test a year` 2009 100 3000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000)
-- pensionable age on 5 April 2010: only 2005 counts (2009-10 is not yet over).
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(1) the number of relevant years that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` `sch 3 test para 6 years` (Date 5 4 2010) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6(1) the number of relevant years that satisfy paragraphs (a) and (b)` `sch 3 test para 6 years` (Date 6 4 2010) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6 the contribution conditions for a child's special allowance are satisfied` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 6 the contribution conditions for a child's special allowance are satisfied` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Part II paragraph 8`

#ASSERT `sch 3 pt II para 8 the first contribution condition is taken to be satisfied` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt II para 8 the first contribution condition is taken to be satisfied` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt II para 8 the first contribution condition is taken to be satisfied` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt II para 8 the first contribution condition is taken to be satisfied` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Earnings factor: which sources count (sub-paragraphs 2(4), 2(5), 5(2)(b), 5(4) and 5A(3))`

-- A source with every component different: Class 1 earnings 1000, credited earnings 200, Class 2 30, Class 3 4, earlier-year contributions 7 (illustrative figures).
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 pt I an earnings factor source`
`sch 3 test a source` MEANS `sch 3 pt I an earnings factor source` OF (`Tax year` OF year), 1000, 200, 30, 4, 7

-- 1987-88 (the year beginning in 1987) is the first year of the first limb; 1986-87 is an earlier year.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I the year is 1987-88 or a subsequent year` (`sch 3 test a source` 1987) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I the year is 1987-88 or a subsequent year` (`sch 3 test a source` 1986) EQUALS FALSE
-- 2(4)(a): Class 1 earnings and Class 2: 1000 + 30 (credited earnings and Class 3 do not count here).
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(4) the earnings factor for the first condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1987) EQUALS 1030
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(4) the earnings factor for the first condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 2010) EQUALS 1030
-- 2(4)(b): an earlier year: the contributions paid, 7.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(4) the earnings factor for the first condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1986) EQUALS 7
-- 2(5)(a): adds earnings credited: 1000 + 200 + 30.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(5) the earnings factor for the second condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1987) EQUALS 1230
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 2(5) the earnings factor for the second condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1986) EQUALS 7
-- 5(2)(b)(i): Class 1 earnings, Class 2 and Class 3: 1000 + 30 + 4; (ii) an earlier year: 7.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2)(b) the earnings factor for the first condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1987) EQUALS 1034
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(2)(b) the earnings factor for the first condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1986) EQUALS 7
-- 5(4)(a): earnings credited too: 1000 + 200 + 30 + 4; (b) an earlier year: 7.
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(4) the earnings factor for the second condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1987) EQUALS 1234
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5(4) the earnings factor for the second condition` (`sch 3 test a source` 1986) EQUALS 7
-- 5A(3): as 5(4).
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(3) the earnings factor` (`sch 3 test a source` 1987) EQUALS 1234
#ASSERT `sch 3 pt I para 5A(3) the earnings factor` (`sch 3 test a source` 1986) EQUALS 7
